You lend jellyfin (port 18096) to everyone in your groups, up to 8 people at once.
jellyfin asks each person to sign in once, with an account you make them. In jellyfin: your picture at the top right, then Dashboard, Users and +; give it a name and a password, tick the libraries they may watch, and Save. Then tell each person theirs.
It signs people in with svrngs. In the app's own settings, choose OpenID Connect, and fill in: issuer http://127.0.0.1:51675/oidc/jellyfin, client id _t6ytzNOllAo64NqDiu7B2Y20JVIWuv4, client secret 9shQnGZxn0OGKdTqvGPlThMyQ3BOxC2qFV86jtE8hwQ.
It is plain http on this computer, not https; it signs tokens with ES256; and it tells the app no email address, because svrngs has none. Copy the secret now: it is not shown again.
svrngs is running here already, so they can open it now.
`svrngs unshare jellyfin` stops lending it.
